<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Lint configuration for the Android app.

  The rule that matters: the vendored CW decoder is exempt.
  `morsekit/cw/` is a line-faithful Kotlin port of the C99 core vendored into the
  iOS app, itself byte-identical to the Carrier Wave firmware's host-tested copy
  (see PROVENANCE.md in that directory). Keeping it diffable against its source
  is worth more than any style opinion lint could have about it, and CLAUDE.md
  says not to reformat, relicense, tidy or relocate it. So lint says nothing
  about that package — a finding there would be an invitation to break the
  provenance.

  Everything else is deliberately left at lint's defaults. Suppress an issue
  here only with a comment saying why, so the file stays a record of decisions
  rather than a place findings go to be forgotten.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="all">
        <ignore path="src/main/java/app/anothermorsetrainer/morsekit/cw" />
    </issue>

</lint>
